{
  "description": "Conformance cases for docs/keyboard-mapping-files.md section 4 (resolution), 3.3 (key names) and 3.4 (platform entries). Every client loads this file, resolves each case's event against the named mapping and the catalogue, and must get the expected result. Event fields: code (W3C), modifiers (host modifiers held, besides the key itself: Shift, Control, Alt, Meta), text (the character the host layout gives with those modifiers, ignoring Control), platform and native (for platform entries; a client runs a case with a platform only if it is its own). Expected: a BBC key by catalogue name and internal key number, with the BBC SHIFT and CTRL the entry or catalogue asks for; or break; or ignored. shift false from character mapping means the BBC SHIFT must be up for that key. A case's mapping is a key of `mappings`, or a file name in this directory (the built-ins).",
